<title>USA: Boeing stock could hit $120 in 1998 - paper.</title>
<headline>Boeing stock could hit $120 in 1998 - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co could see its stock hit $120 in a year or 18.4 times an 1998 earnings estimate of $6.51 a share, according to a stock analyst for the aviation and defence industry at BT Securities Corp, a unit of Bankers Trust.</p>
<p>Wolfgang Demisch was quoted in the weekly financial tabloid Barron's as saying the company nevertheless faced problems from its proposed $13.3 billion merger with McDonnell Douglas Corp.</p>
<p>Demisch predicted higher costs associated with a massive build-up of Boeing's production capacity because of a backlog of orders for its planes.</p>
<p>On Friday, Boeing closed $2 higher at $105-3/8.</p>
